{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ClimaxVolumeMass.KnotOperatorEnergy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ClimaxVolumeMass.KnotOperatorEnergy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorEnergy.energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorEnergy.energy","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/knot-operator-energy.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Energy `|y_λ(q)|` in the absolute-value image, when defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorEnergy.shadowPrice_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorEnergy.shadowPrice_eq","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/knot-operator-energy.lean#L42-L42","doc":"and it IS the LP-dual value for this partition at this `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorEnergy.shadowPrice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorEnergy.shadowPrice","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/knot-operator-energy.lean#L40-L40","doc":"Shadow price `y_λ(q) ∈ R` (algebraic, base-ring-independent). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorEnergy.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorEnergy.mk","kind":"ctor","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/knot-operator-energy.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorEnergy","kind":"structure","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/knot-operator-energy.lean#L17-L44","doc":"**Knot operator energy** at substrate parameter `q : R`.\n\n`dualValue` is the LP-dual value map `(λ, q) ↦ y_λ(q)`, carried as a\n**parameter** — a function of the indexing data — rather than as a free\nfield. That is the repair: `shadowPrice` is now pinned to it by\n`shadowPrice_eq` instead of chosen independently of `partition` and `q`.\n\nUntil 2026-09-06 this was a plain structure with `shadowPrice : R` free,\nplus `axiom KnotOperatorEnergy.shadowPrice_canonical` asserting that two\nrecords agreeing on `partition` and `q` share a `shadowPrice`. **That axiom\nwas false** — `⟨[], 0, 0, none⟩` and `⟨[], 0, 1, none⟩` refute it — and its\nown docstring said why: closing it *\"requires ... a structure refactor\ncarrying the LP-canonicity as a proof field.\"* Bean `qou-9yt9`.\n\nThe determining map is a FUNCTION, not a relation with a uniqueness field:\na structure carrying its own conclusion would be the self-assuming\nprojection AGENTS.md §3b-cond item 5 forbids. Here uniqueness is a\nconsequence of functionality, not an assumption. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:knot-operator-energy","label":"def:knot-operator-energy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/knot-operator-energy.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}